From fa9efa38e5a6133b1beb98cd65db11444edfbf21 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 11:41:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] One shared object layer for shapes, images and styles
 (E10.16, D177-D179)

An object becomes a shared body plus an app-specific anchor, so that the three
apps stop keeping their own copies of what a shape or a picture is.

claudia_core.objects holds ObjectBody (kind, size, style, text, shape, image,
imported, rotation, snap), the Anchor protocol, VisualObject, the ObjectModel
mixin, ObjectSet, ObjectsChanged and the whole object command family as core.*:
DefineShape, ForgetShape, DefineImage, ForgetImage, AddObject, RemoveObject,
MoveObject, ResizeObject, RotateObject, SetText, SetSnap. Each app brings only
its anchor and three methods: containers(), check_anchor, anchor_from_data.
An anchor crosses the log and the wire as plain data, read back by that one
door, so a command stays rebuildable without a model.

Per app: SlideAnchor(slide, x, y) in creates, CellAnchor(sheet, row, col) in
computes, BlockAnchor(block, offset) in composes, which had no object layer at
all before. A cell anchor stays frozen under structural edits on purpose; a
block anchor follows the text, because a character offset that does not move
points at a different word (D179).

creates' styles move from a program-level dict of its own flat Style class into
the document's own core StyleBook, with inheritance, deviation and the core
style commands, as composes already had; computes gains a style book too. This
caught a bug: creates' built-in styles had never been validated, and one font
name in body-text (-apple-system) is in fact refused by ALLOWED_CSS. Shapes say
their background and border as fill/stroke/stroke-width, since a shape is an
outline in a 100 by 100 box and not a rectangle (D178).

The shape format (ShapeDefinition, parse_shape) moves to claudia_core.shapes,
pure and I/O-free; ShapeLibrary, which reads disk, stays in claudia_creates.

On the wire an object is the same in all three apps but for its anchor, and
ObjectSet/ObjectsChanged name one container. The web client gets the matching
split in web/app/lib/objects.ts; geometry.ts needed no change, since it already
worked on frames alone.

Renaming the commands' kind makes logs written before this round unreadable: a
CommandRegistry keys upcasters by (kind, schema) and cannot alias one kind to
another. Chosen deliberately, this being pre-release (D177). State schemas:
creates 4->5, computes 3->4, composes 3->4.

